{{also|har|Har|hár|Hár|hār|hår|hær|Appendix:Variations of "har"}}
==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/hæːr/}}
* {{audio|sv|sv-här.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|sv|æːr|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|sv|non|hér}}, from {{der|sv|gem-pro|*hē₂r}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|sv|adverb}}

# [[here]]; at this time ''or'' at this place
#: '''''Här''' är den.''
#:: Here it is.

=====Usage notes=====
* In several compounds (''[[härkomst]], [[härledning]], ...''), it is also used like the German adverb {{m|de|her||here, to this place}}, which would translate to Swedish {{m|sv|hit||here, to this place}}, rather than ''här''.

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|sv|där}}

